---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

export const prerender = true;

const pageTitle = "Bangladesh Clothing Manufacturing Costs 2026 | SDF Clothing";
const pageDescription = "Complete guide to clothing manufacturing costs in Bangladesh 2026 — labor rates, material prices, overhead, and total cost per garment for international brands.";
const schema = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    "headline": pageTitle,
    "description": pageDescription,
    "author": { "@id": "https://sdfltd.com/#org" },
    "publisher": { "@id": "https://sdfltd.com/#org" },
    "url": "https://sdfltd.com/insights/manufacturing-costs/",
    "mainEntityOfPage": "https://sdfltd.com/insights/manufacturing-costs/"
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Why does cost per piece drop at higher order quantities?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Fixed costs — sampling, cutting setup, factory overhead per batch — get spread across more units. Fabric buying also gets more efficient at higher volumes since bulk fabric orders reduce per-kg pricing. The steepest cost drop typically happens between 300 and 1,000 pieces per style." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Are these prices FOB or landed cost?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "All figures are FOB Chittagong — the factory-gate price before freight, insurance, and import duty. Landed cost adds freight and duty on top, which varies significantly by destination market and product category." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Does GOTS or GRS certified fabric significantly raise the cost?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Certified organic and recycled fabrics generally sit at the higher end of the material cost ranges, reflecting certification and chain-of-custody documentation costs at the mill level, but the increase is usually moderate rather than dramatic." }
      }
    ]
  }
];

---

<BaseLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} schema={schema}>

  <div class="container" style="padding: 3rem 1.5rem 5rem;">

    <!-- Breadcrumb -->
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <p style="font-size: 0.72rem; color: #FFFFFF; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;">
        <a href="/" style="color: #ffffff; text-decoration: none;">Home</a>
        <span style="margin: 0 0.5rem; color: #333;">›</span>
        <a href="/insights/manufacturing-costs" style="color: #aaa; text-decoration: none;">Insights</a>
        <span style="margin: 0 0.5rem; color: #333;">›</span>
        <span style="color: #FFFFFF;">Manufacturing Costs</span>
      </p>
    </nav>

    <article>

      <header style="max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: 3rem; padding-bottom: 2rem; border-top:1px solid #e00;">
        <span style="font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.25em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #e00; display: block; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Cost Guide 2026</span>
        <h1 style="font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.8rem); font-weight: 200; color: #fff; line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; letter-spacing: 0.01em;">
          Bangladesh Clothing Manufacturing Costs
        </h1>
        <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: #aaa; line-height: 1.9; margin: 0;">
          Real cost breakdown for international fashion brands sourcing from Bangladesh. Understand labor rates, material prices, factory overhead, and FOB pricing to plan your margins accurately.
        </p>
      </header>

      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.9; max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        Total FOB cost per garment breaks down into four components that move somewhat independently: labor (the operator's time per piece), fabric and trims (bought by weight or unit, scaling with order size), factory overhead (a relatively fixed per-piece charge regardless of complexity), and shipping (which drops sharply per unit at higher volumes). Understanding how each moves separately — rather than treating "cost" as one number — is what lets a brand negotiate the right lever for their specific order, instead of just asking for a blanket discount.
      </p>

      <!-- Labor -->
      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">Labor Costs</h2>
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 1px; background: #000000; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        <div style="background: #000; padding: 1.75rem; border-top: 0.6px solid #e00;">
          <h3 style="font-size: 0.88rem; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: #fff;">Skilled Garment Workers</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 1.2rem; color: #e00; font-weight: 300; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">$120–180 <span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#FFFFFF;">/month</span></p>
          <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.875rem; margin: 0;">Includes social benefits, overtime rates, and annual bonus as per Bangladesh Labour Law.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #000; padding: 1.75rem; border-top: 0.6px solid #e00;">
          <h3 style="font-size: 0.88rem; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: #fff;">Sewing Machine Operators</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 1.2rem; color: #e00; font-weight: 300; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">$80–120 <span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#FFFFFF;">/month</span></p>
          <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.875rem; margin: 0;">Experienced operators with productivity-based incentives. Minimum wage compliant.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Materials -->
      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">Material Costs</h2>
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 1px; background: #000000; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        <div style="background: #000; padding: 1.75rem; border-top: 0.6px solid #e00;">
          <h3 style="font-size: 0.88rem; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: #fff;">Basic Fabrics</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: #e00; font-weight: 300; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">$2–5 <span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#FFFFFF;">/kg</span></p>
          <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.82rem; margin: 0;">Cotton, polyester, blended. Bulk pricing from 1,000 pcs.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #000; padding: 1.75rem; border-top: 0.6px solid #e00;">
          <h3 style="font-size: 0.88rem; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: #fff;">Premium Materials</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: #e00; font-weight: 300; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">$5–15 <span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#FFFFFF;">/kg</span></p>
          <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.82rem; margin: 0;">Organic cotton, recycled polyester, technical performance fabrics. MOQ 500 pcs.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #000; padding: 1.75rem; border-top: 0.6px solid #e00;">
          <h3 style="font-size: 0.88rem; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: #fff;">Trims &amp; Accessories</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: #e00; font-weight: 300; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">$0.50–5 <span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#FFFFFF;">/unit</span></p>
          <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.82rem; margin: 0;">Zippers, buttons, labels, hang tags, custom packaging. Sourced in-house.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Overhead -->
      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">Overhead &amp; Logistics</h2>
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 1px; background: #000000; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        <div style="background: #000; padding: 1.75rem;">
          <h3 style="font-size: 0.88rem; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: #fff;">Factory Overhead</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: #e00; font-weight: 300; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">$0.80–2.00 <span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#FFFFFF;">/piece</span></p>
          <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.875rem; margin: 0;">Covers utilities, factory management, QC team, compliance reporting, and equipment maintenance.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #000; padding: 1.75rem;">
          <h3 style="font-size: 0.88rem; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: #fff;">FOB Shipping</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: #e00; font-weight: 300; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">$0.50–3.00 <span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#FFFFFF;">/piece</span></p>
          <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.875rem; margin: 0;">FOB Chittagong. Includes customs clearance, export documentation, and certificate of origin.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Total -->
      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">Total Cost Per Garment</h2>

      <div style="background: #000; border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; border-top: 0.6px solid #e00; padding: 2.5rem; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        <p style="font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.25em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #e00; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">FOB Price Range</p>
        <p style="font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 200; color: #fff; line-height: 1; margin-bottom: 1rem;">$3.50 – $12.00</p>
        <p style="color: #aaa; font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.8; max-width: 500px; margin: 0 auto 2rem;">
          Final price depends on garment complexity, fabric choice, order quantity, and customisation. Prices decrease significantly at 1,000+ and 5,000+ units.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact/" style="display: inline-block; background: #e00; color: #fff; padding: 0.9rem 2.5rem; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.15em; text-transform: uppercase; transition: background 0.2s;">
          Get a Detailed Quote →
        </a>
      </div>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">Manufacturing Cost FAQ</h2>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #1a1a1a;padding:1.25rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:0.92rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.6rem;">Why does cost per piece drop at higher order quantities?</h3>
        <p style="color:#aaa;font-size:0.85rem;line-height:1.8;">Fixed costs — sampling, cutting setup, factory overhead per batch — get spread across more units. Fabric buying also gets more efficient at higher volumes since bulk fabric orders reduce per-kg pricing. The steepest cost drop typically happens between 300 and 1,000 pieces per style.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #1a1a1a;padding:1.25rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:0.92rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.6rem;">Are these prices FOB or landed cost?</h3>
        <p style="color:#aaa;font-size:0.85rem;line-height:1.8;">All figures above are FOB Chittagong — the factory-gate price before freight, insurance, and import duty. Landed cost (your actual all-in cost at your warehouse) adds freight and duty on top, which varies significantly by destination market and product category.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.25rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:0.92rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.6rem;">Does GOTS or GRS certified fabric significantly raise the cost?</h3>
        <p style="color:#aaa;font-size:0.85rem;line-height:1.8;">Certified organic and recycled fabrics generally sit at the higher end of the material cost ranges above, reflecting certification and chain-of-custody documentation costs at the mill level, but the increase is usually moderate rather than dramatic — often a smaller factor than fabric weight or construction complexity.</p>
      </div>

    </article>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <div style="text-align: center; padding: 2.5rem; border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; background: #000;">
      <p style="color: #fff; font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; font-weight: 300;">
        Ready to see exact costs for your specific product?
      </p>
      <a href="/contact/" style="display: inline-block; background: transparent; border: 0.6px solid #e00; color: #e00; padding: 0.9rem 2.5rem; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.15em; text-transform: uppercase; transition: background 0.2s, color 0.2s;">
        Contact Our Pricing Team →
      </a>
    </div>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
